<h1>Testing Automation Tool (TAT)</h1>
<p style="font-size: 13pt; color: #4A5568;"><strong>Complete Project Architecture, High-Level Flow & System Blueprint</strong></p>
<p><strong>Platform:</strong> Spring Boot 3.5 &bull; Java 21 &bull; PostgreSQL &bull; JWT Security &bull; MapStruct &bull; Apache POI</p>

<div class="highlight-box">
<strong>Executive Summary:</strong> The <strong>Testing Automation Tool (TAT)</strong> is an enterprise Quality Assurance (QA) lifecycle management platform. It manages the entire testing pipeline: from project inception, feature slicing, manual and bulk Excel test case creation, execution cycles, real-time defect tracking with audit history, file attachment repositories, and instant team chat, up to executive KPI analytics for engineering managers.
</div>

<h2>1. High-Level System Architecture & Flow</h2>

<p>The system is organized into a clean 5-tier enterprise layered architecture:</p>

<table style="margin-top: 10px;">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th style="width: 20%;">Layer</th>
            <th style="width: 35%;">Key Components</th>
            <th style="width: 45%;">Responsibilities</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>1. Client / UI</strong></td>
            <td>Web Portal, SPA, Swagger UI, Excel Uploads</td>
            <td>Sends HTTP REST requests with Bearer JWT tokens; renders dashboards and reports.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>2. Security & Gateway</strong></td>
            <td><code>JwtAuthenticationFilter</code>, <code>SecurityConfig</code></td>
            <td>Validates JWT tokens, extracts claims, enforces Role-Based Access Control (RBAC).</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>3. API / Controller Layer</strong></td>
            <td>10 REST Controllers (Project, Feature, TestCase, Bug, Comment, Dashboard, Attachment, etc.)</td>
            <td>Validates incoming DTOs (<code>@Valid</code>), routes requests, returns unified <code>ApiResponse&lt;T&gt;</code>.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>4. Business Service Layer</strong></td>
            <td>Service Interfaces & Implementations (<code>ProjectServiceImpl</code>, <code>TestCaseServiceImpl</code>, etc.)</td>
            <td>Contains core business rules, status cascades, duration calculators, and Excel parsers.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>5. Persistence & Database</strong></td>
            <td>Spring Data JPA, Hibernate, PostgreSQL, Dynamic Specifications</td>
            <td>Stores entities, audit logs, binary file blobs, search indices, and execution metrics.</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h2>2. Core Domain Hierarchy (Parent-to-Child Relationship)</h2>

<p>The entire system revolves around a hierarchical data structure. Every item has a strict parent-child relationship with automatic cascading behavior:</p>

<div class="highlight-box">
<p style="font-size: 12pt; margin: 4px 0;"><strong>Hierarchy Tree:</strong></p>
<p style="margin: 4px 0; font-family: monospace;">
🏢 <strong>PROJECT</strong> (e.g. Mobile Banking App, Web Portal)<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;└── 📁 <strong>FEATURE</strong> (e.g. Login, Fund Transfer, Bill Payment)<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;└── 📝 <strong>TEST CASE</strong> (e.g. Verify OTP validation on valid phone number)<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;├── ⚡ <strong>TESTING EXECUTION</strong> (Status: Pass, Fail, Norun, Descope)<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;└── 🐛 <strong>BUG / DEFECT</strong> (e.g. OTP not sent for +91 numbers)<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;├── 💬 <strong>COMMENTS</strong> (Live team chat & updates)<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;└── 📎 <strong>ATTACHMENTS</strong> (Screenshots, screen recordings, logs)
</p>
</div>

<h3>Cascading Rules & Soft Deletion:</h3>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Project Deactivation:</strong> When a Manager deactivates a Project, all associated Features, Test Cases, and Bugs are automatically deactivated.</li>
    <li><strong>Feature Deactivation:</strong> Deactivating a Feature suspends all underlying Test Cases.</li>
    <li><strong>Soft Delete:</strong> Entities have <code>isDeleted = true</code> to preserve historical audit data while hiding them from active queries.</li>
</ul>

