<h2>4. Detailed Core Modules Breakdown</h2>

<h3>4.1 Authentication & User Approval Lifecycle</h3>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Registration:</strong> New users sign up with username, email, and password. By default, accounts are in a <code>PENDING</code> inactive state.</li>
    <li><strong>Manager Confirmation:</strong> A Manager reviews pending users via <code>/manager/users/pending</code> and confirms their role (e.g. TESTER, MANAGER) or rejects them.</li>
    <li><strong>Secure Login:</strong> Generates a short-lived <strong>Access Token</strong> (JWT) and a persisted <strong>Refresh Token</strong> for seamless session rotation.</li>
</ul>

<h3>4.2 Project & Feature Slicing</h3>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Projects:</strong> Groups software products by Name, Region (e.g. US, EU, APAC), and Status.</li>
    <li><strong>Features:</strong> Slices projects into testable deliverables with sprint numbers, feature versions, and custom duration timers (Days, Hours, Minutes, or Live Start/End timers).</li>
</ul>

<h3>4.3 Test Case Management & Bulk Excel Processing</h3>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Manual Creation:</strong> Single test cases with Preconditions, Test Data, Execution Steps, UI Validations, and DB Validations.</li>
    <li><strong>Dynamic Excel Template:</strong> Custom generator (<code>/testcases/template/{projectId}/{featureId}</code>) creates pre-formatted <code>.xlsx</code> templates with dropdowns and column guides.</li>
    <li><strong>Bulk Upload Engine:</strong> High-performance Apache POI reader that parses hundreds of test cases in a single transaction, validating mandatory fields and providing row-by-row error reporting.</li>
</ul>

<h3>4.4 Test Execution Engine</h3>
<ul>
    <li>Tracks execution status for every test case: <code>PASS</code>, <code>FAIL</code>, <code>NORUN</code>, <code>DESCOPE</code>, <code>BLOCKED</code>.</li>
    <li>Automatically increments failure metrics and links directly to defect creation when a test case fails.</li>
</ul>

<h3>4.5 Bug & Defect Tracking System</h3>
<ul>
    <li>Auto-generated unique format IDs (e.g., <code>BUG-1001</code>).</li>
    <li>Captures Severity (<code>CRITICAL</code>, <code>HIGH</code>, <code>MEDIUM</code>, <code>LOW</code>) and Priority (<code>P1</code>, <code>P2</code>, <code>P3</code>, <code>P4</code>).</li>
    <li><strong>Occurrence Counter:</strong> Tracks how many times a bug reproduces across test runs.</li>
    <li><strong>Bug History:</strong> Maintains an immutable audit trail of all status changes (e.g., <code>OPEN</code> ➔ <code>IN_PROGRESS</code> ➔ <code>RESOLVED</code> ➔ <code>CLOSED</code>).</li>
</ul>

<h3>4.6 Real-Time Comments & Collaboration</h3>
<ul>
    <li>Live communication thread attached to any bug.</li>
    <li>Allows testers, developers, and managers to discuss reproduction steps and fixes in real time.</li>
</ul>

<h3>4.7 Enterprise Attachment Repository</h3>
<ul>
    <li>Supports multi-level attachments: Attach files directly to a <strong>Project</strong>, <strong>Feature</strong>, <strong>TestCase</strong>, or <strong>Bug</strong>.</li>
    <li>Stores files securely as BLOBs with metadata (file size, MIME type, upload timestamp, author).</li>
    <li><strong>Bulk ZIP Downloader:</strong> Automatically packages multiple attachments into a single downloadable <code>.zip</code> file with duplicate filename resolution.</li>
</ul>

<h3>4.8 Executive & Manager Analytics Dashboards</h3>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Overview Dashboard:</strong> High-level cards for Total Projects, Active Features, Test Case Execution Progress, Defect Severity Distribution, and Failing Features.</li>
    <li><strong>Project Deep-Dive:</strong> Pass/Fail ratios, descope counts, bug density per feature, and tester productivity.</li>
    <li><strong>Feature Deep-Dive:</strong> Execution percentage, open vs resolved bugs, and average test cycle time.</li>
</ul>

<h2>5. Standardized API Architecture (Unified Responses)</h2>

<div class="success-box">
<strong>Unified API Design Philosophy:</strong>
All <code>GET</code>, <code>POST</code>, and <code>PUT</code> endpoints return the <strong>exact same standardized response DTO</strong> wrapped in a universal <code>ApiResponse&lt;T&gt;</code> envelope.
</div>

<table>
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th>Module</th>
            <th>HTTP POST (Create)</th>
            <th>HTTP GET (Read by ID)</th>
            <th>HTTP PUT (Update)</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Project</strong></td>
            <td><code>ApiResponse&lt;ProjectResponse&gt;</code></td>
            <td><code>ApiResponse&lt;ProjectResponse&gt;</code></td>
            <td><code>ApiResponse&lt;ProjectResponse&gt;</code></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Feature</strong></td>
            <td><code>ApiResponse&lt;FeatureResponse&gt;</code></td>
            <td><code>ApiResponse&lt;FeatureResponse&gt;</code></td>
            <td><code>ApiResponse&lt;FeatureResponse&gt;</code></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>TestCase</strong></td>
            <td><code>ApiResponse&lt;TestCaseExecutionResponse&gt;</code></td>
            <td><code>ApiResponse&lt;TestCaseResponse&gt;</code></td>
            <td><code>ApiResponse&lt;TestCaseResponse&gt;</code></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Bug</strong></td>
            <td><code>ApiResponse&lt;BugResponse&gt;</code></td>
            <td><code>ApiResponse&lt;BugResponse&gt;</code></td>
            <td><code>ApiResponse&lt;BugResponse&gt;</code></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Comment</strong></td>
            <td><code>ApiResponse&lt;CommentResponse&gt;</code></td>
            <td><code>ApiResponse&lt;List&lt;CommentResponse&gt;&gt;</code></td>
            <td><code>ApiResponse&lt;CommentResponse&gt;</code></td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h3>Standard JSON Envelope Example:</h3>
<pre>
{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Operation completed successfully",
  "data": {
    "project": {
      "projectId": 10,
      "projectName": "Payment Gateway 2.0",
      "status": "ACTIVE",
      "region": "GLOBAL",
      "version": 1
    },
    "audit": {
      "createdBy": 2,
      "createdByName": "alex_manager",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-07T08:00:00Z"
    }
  },
  "timestamp": "2026-10-07T08:00:00.123Z"
}
</pre>

<h2>6. End-to-End QA Workflow</h2>

<ol>
    <li><strong>Step 1 (Manager Setup):</strong> Manager logs in, creates a new <strong>Project</strong> (e.g. <i>"E-Commerce App"</i>), and slices it into <strong>Features</strong> (e.g. <i>"Checkout Flow"</i>).</li>
    <li><strong>Step 2 (Test Authoring):</strong> Tester downloads the dynamic Excel template, fills out 50 test cases offline, and uploads the spreadsheet via <code>POST /testcases/upload</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>Step 3 (Test Execution):</strong> Tester executes test cases sequentially, marking results as <code>PASS</code> or <code>FAIL</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>Step 4 (Bug Filing):</strong> On test failure, Tester logs a <strong>Bug</strong> (linked to the test case), attaches error screenshots, and posts comments.</li>
    <li><strong>Step 5 (Resolution & Retest):</strong> Developer reviews bug comments, fixes the issue, updates bug status to <code>RESOLVED</code>, and Tester re-runs the test case to mark it <code>PASS</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>Step 6 (Executive Review):</strong> Manager opens <code>/manager/dashboard/overview</code> to view real-time release readiness, defect trends, and sign off on deployment.</li>
</ol>

